13:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose-custom max-w-none","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["# Email Frequency Management: Finding the Sweet Spot Without Losing Subscribers"]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["> *Send too many emails and risk unsubscribes; send too few and risk being forgotten. This guide covers frequency optimization strategies -- backed by data, tested in the wild, and designed for real-world results.*"]}],["$","p","4",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["In the inbox wars, frequency is your silent strategist. Too aggressive? You're labeled spammy, ignored, or -- worse -- unsubscribed from. Too passive? Your brand fades into digital oblivion, buried under newsletters from competitors who *did* show up. So how often *should* you email your list?"]}],["$","p","6",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Spoiler: There's no universal \"one-size-fits-all\" answer -- but there *is* a data-informed sweet spot. And it's more nuanced (and actionable) than you think."]}],["$","hr","8",{"className":"border-[#5F1E1E] my-8"}],["$","h2","10",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"📊 The Data Doesn't Lie: What Benchmarks Reveal"}],["$","p","12",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Let's start with cold, hard numbers from trusted industry sources:"]}],["$","p","14",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Mailchimp's 2023 Email Marketing Benchmark Report"}]," found that brands sending ",["$","strong","3",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"1-2 emails per week"}]," achieved the highest average open rate (",["$","strong","5",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"21.4%"}],") and click-through rate (",["$","strong","7",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"2.7%"}],") across all industries -- outperforming both daily senders (16.8% open rate) and monthly-only senders (14.1% open rate)."]}],["$","p","15",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Omnisend's 2024 E-commerce Email Trends Report"}]," revealed that online retailers emailing ",["$","strong","3",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"twice weekly"}]," saw ",["$","strong","5",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"32% higher revenue per subscriber"}]," than those emailing just once a month -- but those emailing *daily* experienced a ",["$","strong","7",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"23% increase in unsubscribe rates"}]," YoY."]}],["$","p","16",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- A landmark 2022 study by HubSpot tracked 12,000+ B2B campaigns and found that ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"segmented, behavior-triggered emails sent at variable frequencies (e.g., 3x/week to engaged users, 1x/week to dormant ones) drove 58% more conversions"}]," than uniform weekly blasts."]}],["$","p","18",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["The takeaway? ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Consistency beats volume. Relevance trumps rhythm."}],""]}],["$","hr","20",{"className":"border-[#5F1E1E] my-8"}],["$","h2","22",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"🔍 Why \"Optimal Frequency\" Is Unique to *Your* Audience"}],"$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32",